    {
      "page_title": "Volumes: Types, Mounts and subPath",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "A __Volume__ is a ==directory==, backed by some medium, that every container in the pod can mount — its lifetime is the **pod's**, not the container's.",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Definition and Lifetime",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Pod-scoped: shared by ==all containers== in the pod",
            "Container **crash + restart** keeps the data",
            "Pod **deleted** destroys it (ephemeral types)",
            "Not a cluster object — no `kubectl get volumes`"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Example : nginx container OOM-kills and restarts; the `emptyDir` at `/cache` still holds yesterday's files. Delete the pod and the directory is {red:gone}.",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "pink"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Declare, Then Mount",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "yaml",
          "lines": [
            "spec:",
            "  volumes:            # pod level",
            "  - name: logs",
            "    emptyDir: {}",
            "  containers:",
            "  - name: app",
            "    volumeMounts:     # per container",
            "    - name: logs",
            "      mountPath: /var/log"
          ],
          "note": "one volume, many mountPaths"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. The Volume Types",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Type",
            "Holds",
            "Note"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`emptyDir`",
              "scratch dir",
              "empty at schedule"
            ],
            [
              "`medium: Memory`",
              "tmpfs in RAM",
              "counts vs mem limit"
            ],
            [
              "`hostPath`",
              "node directory",
              "node-affine, **risky**"
            ],
            [
              "`configMap` / `secret`",
              "injected data",
              "read-only, not storage"
            ],
            [
              "`ephemeral`",
              "inline PVC",
              "PVC semantics, pod life"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "solid"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "{icon:kubernetes} `downwardAPI` / `projected` also inject — __never__ persist",
            "`hostPath` mostly for node agents: log shippers, {icon:prometheus} node-exporter",
            "`ephemeral.volumeClaimTemplate` = a PVC born and **deleted** with the pod"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Example: Sidecar Log Pattern",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              {
                "text": "app container",
                "sub": "writes /var/log",
                "ink": "blue"
              },
              {
                "text": "emptyDir: logs",
                "sub": "one shared dir",
                "ink": "green"
              },
              {
                "text": "fluent-bit sidecar",
                "sub": "reads /logs, ships",
                "ink": "orange"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. subPath and subPathExpr",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "yaml",
          "lines": [
            "volumeMounts:",
            "- name: cfg",
            "  mountPath: /etc/n.conf",
            "  subPath: nginx.conf   # 1 file",
            "- name: logs",
            "  mountPath: /data",
            "  subPathExpr: $(POD_NAME)"
          ],
          "note": "subPathExpr expands env vars"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Key rule",
          "text": "Volume = **pod lifetime**. Anything that must outlive the pod needs a PVC — page 4."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "A ==PersistentVolume== is a __cluster-scoped__ object that represents a **real** piece of storage — cut by an admin by hand, or minted by a __driver__ dynamically."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "kubernetes",
      "subtitle": "emptyDir, hostPath, projected and inline ephemeral"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Inline Ephemeral PVCs and emptyDir Size Limits",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Example : admin makes `pv-nfs-01` (50Gi, RWX) → phase `Available` → PVC `pgdata` in ns `prod` claims it → `Bound`, `claimRef: prod/pgdata`.",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "pink"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Inline Ephemeral PVC",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "yaml",
          "lines": [
            "volumes:",
            "- name: scratch",
            "  ephemeral:",
            "    volumeClaimTemplate:",
            "      spec:",
            "        accessModes: [ReadWriteOnce]",
            "        resources:",
            "          requests: {storage: 10Gi}"
          ],
          "note": "PVC named <pod>-scratch, dies with pod"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Capping emptyDir",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`emptyDir: {sizeLimit: 2Gi}` — over it, the pod is ==evicted==",
            "Disk-backed emptyDir counts against node **ephemeral-storage**",
            "Set `ephemeral-storage` requests + limits per container",
            "`medium: Memory` without `sizeLimit` can eat half the node RAM"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "kubernetes",
      "subtitle": "emptyDir, hostPath, projected and inline ephemeral"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Mount Traps and the PersistentVolume Spec",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Mount over a **non-empty** dir and the original files are ==hidden==, not merged",
            "`emptyDir` with `medium: Memory` eats the container **memory limit** — OOMKill",
            "`hostPath` pins the pod to one node and hands it the host filesystem",
            "Treating `configMap` as writable storage — the mount is __read-only__"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Definition",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Not namespaced: `kubectl get pv` needs **no** `-n`",
            "Claimed by ==exactly one PVC== at a time — `claimRef`",
            "Made by an admin (static) or a provisioner (dynamic)",
            "Outlives the pod, the claim, even the namespace"
          ],
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Key Spec Fields"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Field",
            "Meaning"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`capacity.storage`",
              "size hint, `50Gi`"
            ],
            [
              "`accessModes`",
              "RWO / ROX / RWX"
            ],
            [
              "`persistentVolume` `ReclaimPolicy`",
              "Delete / Retain"
            ],
            [
              "`storageClassName`",
              "must **equal** PVC's"
            ],
            [
              "`csi` / `nfs` / `local`",
              "the driver source"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "solid"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Phases and Reclaim"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              {
                "text": "Available",
                "sub": "free, no claim"
              },
              {
                "text": "Bound",
                "sub": "one PVC holds it"
              },
              {
                "text": "Released",
                "sub": "PVC gone, data still there",
                "ink": "orange"
              },
              {
                "text": "Failed",
                "sub": "reclaim errored",
                "ink": "red"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Policy",
            "What happens",
            "Data"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Delete",
              "backing disk destroyed",
              "gone"
            ],
            [
              "Retain",
              "PV sits `Released`",
              "kept"
            ],
            [
              "Recycle",
              "deprecated, **removed**",
              "—"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 1,
          "frame": "solid"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Static PV: NFS"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "yaml",
          "lines": [
            "kind: PersistentVolume",
            "spec:",
            "  capacity: {storage: 50Gi}",
            "  accessModes: [ReadWriteMany]",
            "  storageClassName: \"\"  # static",
            "  nfs: {server: 10.0.2.14,",
            "        path: /exports/pgdata}"
          ],
          "note": "matched by a PVC asking 50Gi RWX"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "nodeAffinity — the local rule",
          "items": [
            "Pins the PV to nodes that can __reach__ the disk",
            "**Mandatory** for `local:` volumes",
            "Scheduler reads it to place the pod",
            "Cloud CSI sets zone affinity for you"
          ],
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "A PVC is a __namespaced request__ for storage that the control plane satisfies with a PV — the ==binding== is exclusive, one-to-one and permanent."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "volumeMode",
            "Filesystem (default)",
            "Block"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "pod field",
              "`volumeMounts`",
              "`volumeDevices`"
            ],
            [
              "given as",
              "formatted dir",
              "raw device"
            ],
            [
              "use for",
              "most apps",
              "DB owns layout"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "solid"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "kubernetes",
      "subtitle": "emptyDir, hostPath, projected and inline ephemeral"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "PV Mistakes and the PVC Binding Contract",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Putting a PV in a namespace — it is **cluster**-scoped",
            "Reading `capacity` as a quota — the disk sets real size",
            "Deleting a bound PV: `kubernetes.io/pv-protection` holds it",
            "`local` PV with no `nodeAffinity` — pod lands disk-less",
            "Waiting for a `Released` PV to re-bind on its own"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Key rule",
          "text": "One PV, one PVC, no namespace. `capacity` only __matches__ — Retain keeps your data but leaves the PV **stuck** until an admin clears `claimRef`."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Definition",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A ==PVC== asks for **size**, **accessModes** and a **class**",
            "Namespaced object; the PV it binds is cluster-scoped",
            "PV/PVC split mirrors {blue:node}/{blue:pod}: infra vs request",
            "App author names a claim, never the backend"
          ],
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Example : dev writes `20Gi, RWO, gp3` and never learns if the disk is __EBS__, __CephFS__ or __NFS__ — the claim hides it.",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "pink"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Binding Contract",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "PVC asks",
            "PV must be",
            "Rule"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`storage: 20Gi`",
              "capacity ≥ 20Gi",
              "larger OK, **wasted**"
            ],
            [
              "`accessModes`",
              "includes all",
              "not a subset"
            ],
            [
              "`storageClassName`",
              "equal string",
              "no fuzzy match"
            ],
            [
              "phase Pending",
              "phase Available",
              "then both Bound"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 0,
          "frame": "solid"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "PV controller does the match — one PV, one PVC, **exclusive**",
            "A 20Gi claim on a 100Gi PV keeps all 100Gi; never split",
            "No PV + no class that can provision = ==Pending forever==",
            "`kubectl describe pvc` events name the reason"
          ],
          "style": "dot"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Example: Claim + Deployment",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "yaml",
          "lines": [
            "kind: PersistentVolumeClaim",
            "metadata: {name: pgdata}",
            "spec:",
            "  accessModes: [ReadWriteOnce]",
            "  storageClassName: gp3",
            "  resources:",
            "    requests: {storage: 20Gi}"
          ],
          "note": "namespace shop"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Forcing the Match",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Field on PVC",
            "Effect"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`volumeName: pv-8f2`",
              "pin one exact PV"
            ],
            [
              "`selector.matchLabels`",
              "pick from static pool"
            ],
            [
              "neither + no class",
              "stays **Pending**"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "solid"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Key Rule",
          "text": "Same __namespace__, capacity ≥ request, modes contained, class string equal — miss one and the claim sits Pending."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. The Four Access Modes",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "A PV declares which __accessModes__ it supports; a PVC requests one. Binding needs the mode to be ==in the PV's list==, nothing more.",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "kubernetes",
      "subtitle": "emptyDir, hostPath, projected and inline ephemeral"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Mounting a Claim and the Four Access Modes",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "yaml",
          "lines": [
            "volumes:                # pod spec",
            "- name: data",
            "  persistentVolumeClaim:",
            "    claimName: pgdata",
            "volumeMounts:           # in ctr",
            "- {name: data, mountPath: /data}"
          ],
          "note": "pod and PVC share one namespace"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Reading the Output",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "console",
          "lines": [
            "$ kubectl get pvc,pv",
            "pvc/pgdata  Bound    pv-8f2  20Gi",
            "pvc/logs    Pending  <none>",
            "pv/pv-8f2   Bound    shop/pgdata"
          ],
          "note": "PV row shows the owning namespace"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Common Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Deleting a Deployment does **not** delete its PVC — cost surprise",
            "Deleting a PVC in use only marks it ==Terminating==",
            "`kubernetes.io/pvc-protection` finalizer waits on the pod",
            "Pod in another namespace cannot mount the claim",
            "Guessing instead of reading `describe pvc` events"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Mode",
            "Short",
            "Who may mount"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "ReadWriteOnce",
              "RWO",
              "one **node**, read-write"
            ],
            [
              "ReadOnlyMany",
              "ROX",
              "many nodes, read-only"
            ],
            [
              "ReadWriteMany",
              "RWX",
              "many nodes, read-write"
            ],
            [
              "ReadWriteOncePod",
              "RWOP",
              "exactly one **pod**, cluster-wide"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 3
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "RWO is the default for block disks: {icon:ebs} EBS, GCE PD",
            "RWX needs a shared filesystem: NFS, CephFS, {icon:efs} EFS, Azure Files",
            "RWOP is ==CSI-only== — the real mutual-exclusion guarantee",
            "`kubectl get pv` prints them as RWO / ROX / RWX / RWOP"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "RWO = one NODE, not one pod",
          "text": "Three pods on the __same node__ can all mount one RWO volume read-write. No locking. People expecting exclusivity get silent double writes — use {red:RWOP} if you need one pod."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Block vs File vs Object",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Backing",
            "Mode",
            "Trade-off"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Block disk",
              "RWO",
              "fast, single-attach"
            ],
            [
              "File share",
              "RWX",
              "slower, POSIX quirks"
            ],
            [
              "Object (S3)",
              "—",
              "**not a volume**"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "solid"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Object storage has no POSIX semantics — app talks HTTP, not `mount`",
            "File shares fake locking and `chown`; databases hate them",
            "Modes are a __scheduling contract__, not enforcement — the **driver** decides on a double mount"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "ink": "red"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "kubernetes",
      "subtitle": "PV — the admin-side half of the storage contract"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Access Mode Traps, Topology and the StorageClass",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "RollingUpdate starts the new pod __before__ the old one dies — both want the RWO disk",
            "Fix: `strategy: {type: Recreate}` on the Deployment",
            "Or use a **StatefulSet** — ordered replace, one pod per PVC",
            "Requesting RWX from an EBS class: PVC Pending forever"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Topology and Binding Mode",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "yaml",
          "lines": [
            "volumeBindingMode:",
            "  WaitForFirstConsumer",
            "# vs Immediate (binds now)"
          ],
          "note": "set on the StorageClass, not the PVC"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "chain",
          "spec": {
            "title": "WaitForFirstConsumer flow",
            "steps": [
              {
                "text": "PVC created",
                "note": "stays Pending — on purpose",
                "ink": "orange"
              },
              {
                "text": "Pod scheduled to node in zone us-east-1b",
                "note": "scheduler picks first",
                "ink": "blue"
              },
              {
                "text": "Driver provisions disk in that zone",
                "note": "reads topology label",
                "ink": "green"
              },
              {
                "text": "PV created and bound",
                "note": "pod and disk co-located",
                "ink": "green"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`Immediate` binds at claim time — disk may land in ==the wrong zone==",
            "A zonal disk pins the pod: no node in that zone, pod stays Pending",
            "`topology.kubernetes.io/zone` is how scheduler and driver agree",
            "Multi-zone clusters: {green:always} WaitForFirstConsumer"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Mistakes and Failure Modes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "lines": [
            "Multi-Attach error for volume",
            "\"pvc-8f2a...\" Volume is already",
            "exclusively attached to one node"
          ],
          "note": "RWO volume, two pods, two nodes"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky-pink",
          "title": "Rule of thumb",
          "text": "One writer on a block disk. Many writers means {pink:RWX file share} or an app that shards its own data."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "A ==StorageClass== is a named profile of storage — a __provisioner__ plus __parameters__ — that lets a PVC ask for a disk and get one **created** on demand, no admin in the loop.",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Definition",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Cluster-scoped, no namespace, referenced by name",
            "`provisioner` = which CSI driver builds the volume",
            "`parameters` = driver-specific knobs (type, iops)",
            "One class per tier of storage you sell"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Mechanism",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "chain",
          "spec": {
            "title": "Dynamic Provisioning Path",
            "steps": [
              {
                "text": "PVC names a class",
                "note": "phase: Pending",
                "ink": "blue"
              },
              {
                "text": "external-provisioner sees it",
                "note": "sidecar watches claims"
              },
              {
                "text": "CreateVolume on driver",
                "note": "real disk in the cloud",
                "ink": "orange"
              },
              {
                "text": "PV created + bound",
                "note": "phase: Bound",
                "ink": "green"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`mountOptions`: passed to every PV it makes",
            "`allowedTopologies`: pin zones the disk may land in"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky-pink",
          "title": "Empty vs omitted",
          "text": "`storageClassName: \"\"` **disables** provisioning and forces static matching. Omitting the field is the opposite — it takes the default class."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "__CSI__ is a ==vendor-neutral gRPC spec== so storage vendors ship {green:out-of-tree} drivers instead of patching Kubernetes itself.",
          "ink": "black"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "kubernetes",
      "subtitle": "The Namespaced Request for Storage"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "StorageClass Fields, Tiers and Why CSI Exists",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Fields",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Field",
            "Meaning"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`provisioner`",
              "driver name, immutable"
            ],
            [
              "`parameters`",
              "type, iops, fsType, encrypted"
            ],
            [
              "`reclaimPolicy`",
              "Delete (default) or Retain"
            ],
            [
              "`allowVolumeExpansion`",
              "lets PVCs grow later"
            ],
            [
              "`volumeBindingMode`",
              "Immediate / WaitForFirstConsumer"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "solid"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "yaml",
          "lines": [
            "kind: StorageClass",
            "metadata:",
            "  name: fast-ssd",
            "provisioner: ebs.csi.aws.com",
            "parameters:",
            "  type: gp3",
            "  iops: \"6000\"",
            "  encrypted: \"true\"",
            "reclaimPolicy: Delete",
            "allowVolumeExpansion: true",
            "volumeBindingMode:",
            "  WaitForFirstConsumer"
          ],
          "note": "gp3 tier, grows, binds where pod lands"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "The default class",
          "text": "Annotation `storageclass.kubernetes.io/is-default-class: \"true\"` marks it. A PVC with **no** `storageClassName` gets that class."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Static vs Dynamic",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "",
            "Static",
            "Dynamic"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Who makes PV",
              "admin, by hand",
              "provisioner"
            ],
            [
              "Best for",
              "pre-existing data",
              "self-service"
            ],
            [
              "Cost",
              "control, toil",
              "less control"
            ],
            [
              "`storageClassName`",
              "`\"\"` or matching",
              "class name"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 3,
          "frame": "solid"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Common Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "**Two** default classes, or none — claims stay Pending or land in the wrong tier",
            "Editing a class — most fields are __immutable__; make a new one and migrate",
            "Forgetting `reclaimPolicy` is inherited at __provisioning time__ — later edits do not touch old PVs",
            "Leaving the Delete default on prod — `kubectl delete pvc` destroys the disk"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "Tiered classes",
                "lines": [],
                "text": "fast-ssd / standard / cheap-cold — app teams pick by __name__, never by backend",
                "ink": "green"
              },
              {
                "title": "Check the cluster",
                "lines": [],
                "code": [
                  "kubectl get sc",
                  "# exactly one (default)"
                ],
                "ink": "blue"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Why CSI Exists",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "In-tree plugins put **vendor code** inside kubelet + controller-manager",
            "Every driver fix needed a full ==Kubernetes release==",
            "CSI migration rerouted in-tree calls to CSI drivers",
            "Legacy in-tree plugins (AWS, GCE, Cinder) are now {red:removed}"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Sidecars = the glue",
          "items": [
            "`external-provisioner` watches **PVCs**",
            "`external-attacher` makes VolumeAttachments",
            "`external-resizer` drives expansion",
            "`external-snapshotter` drives snapshots",
            "`livenessprobe` reports driver health"
          ],
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`kubectl get volumeattachment` — is one even created?",
            "**external-attacher** logs on the controller pod",
            "Node driver logs on __that__ node for mount errors"
          ],
          "style": "number",
          "ink": "black"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "kubernetes",
      "subtitle": "RWO, ROX, RWX, RWOP and where the disk lives"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Inside a CSI Driver: Services, Objects, Stuck Attaches",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Attach vs Mount",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              {
                "text": "ControllerPublish",
                "sub": "device onto node",
                "ink": "orange"
              },
              {
                "text": "NodeStage",
                "sub": "format + mount once/node",
                "ink": "blue"
              },
              {
                "text": "NodePublish",
                "sub": "bind-mount per pod",
                "ink": "green"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "$ kubectl get csidrivers",
            "NAME            ATTACHREQ  MODES",
            "ebs.csi.aws.com true   Persistent",
            "secrets-store.csi.k8s.io false Ephemeral"
          ],
          "note": "Ephemeral mode = inline, no PVC"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Three gRPC Services",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Service",
            "Runs on",
            "Key RPCs"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Identity",
              "both",
              "GetPluginInfo, capabilities"
            ],
            [
              "Controller",
              "controller pod",
              "CreateVolume, DeleteVolume"
            ],
            [
              "Controller",
              "controller pod",
              "ControllerPublish (attach)"
            ],
            [
              "Node",
              "every node",
              "NodeStage, NodePublish"
            ],
            [
              "Node",
              "every node",
              "NodeUnpublish, NodeExpand"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "solid"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Deployment Shape",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "chain",
          "spec": {
            "title": "Driver Layout",
            "steps": [
              {
                "text": "Controller Deployment",
                "note": "driver + sidecars, 1-2 replicas",
                "ink": "purple"
              },
              {
                "text": "UNIX socket /csi/csi.sock",
                "note": "sidecars talk to driver locally",
                "ink": "blue"
              },
              {
                "text": "Node DaemonSet",
                "note": "driver + node-driver-registrar",
                "ink": "green"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. The Two Objects",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Object",
            "Declares"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "CSIDriver",
              "attachRequired, podInfoOnMount"
            ],
            [
              "CSIDriver",
              "fsGroupPolicy, volumeLifecycleModes"
            ],
            [
              "CSINode",
              "drivers a node runs + topology keys"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "solid"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Inline CSI volumes",
          "text": "`volumeLifecycleModes: [Ephemeral]` lets drivers like {green:secrets-store} mount data straight into the pod spec — ==no PVC, no PV== at all."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Reading a Stuck Attach",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "yaml",
          "lines": [
            "kubectl get volumeattachment",
            "spec:",
            "  nodeName: ip-10-0-3-17",
            "  attacher: ebs.csi.aws.com",
            "status:",
            "  attached: false   # <- stuck here"
          ],
          "note": "attached:false = controller side"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Assuming every driver attaches — `attachRequired: false` skips it",
            "Debugging node logs when the RPC never left the controller",
            "Expecting NodeStage per pod — it runs {red:once per node}",
            "Deleting the CSIDriver object: breaks mounts on live pods"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "A bound PVC is not frozen: it can __grow in place__, be copied to a ==point-in-time snapshot==, or be __cloned__ live — all three ride on the {blue:CSI} driver, none of them shrink.",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Driver age",
            "Filesystem step",
            "Pod"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Modern CSI",
              "online",
              "stays up"
            ],
            [
              "Older CSI",
              "offline only",
              "must restart"
            ],
            [
              "Block mode",
              "app resizes",
              "app's job"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "solid"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Example : restore with `dataSource` — a PVC of ==at least the snapshot's size==; smaller stays **Pending** forever.",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "pink"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "kubernetes",
      "subtitle": "Storage as a Named Profile"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Resizing, Snapshot Objects and Live Clones",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Volume Expansion",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Edit `spec.resources.requests.storage` on the **PVC**",
            "Class must set `allowVolumeExpansion: true` — else rejected",
            "__Shrinking is never supported__: new smaller PVC + copy data",
            "Trust ==status.capacity==, not `spec` — spec is only the ask"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Two-Stage Resize",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "chain",
          "spec": {
            "title": "Who grows what",
            "steps": [
              {
                "text": "external-resizer sees bigger request",
                "note": "sidecar watches PVC",
                "ink": "blue"
              },
              {
                "text": "ControllerExpandVolume",
                "note": "backend disk 20Gi → 50Gi",
                "ink": "purple"
              },
              {
                "text": "NodeExpandVolume (kubelet)",
                "note": "resize2fs / xfs_growfs",
                "ink": "green"
              },
              {
                "text": "status.capacity updated",
                "note": "only now is it real",
                "ink": "orange"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Example: 20Gi → 50Gi",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "kubectl patch pvc pgdata -p \\",
            "  '{\"spec\":{\"resources\":{\"requests\"",
            "   :{\"storage\":\"50Gi\"}}}}'",
            "kubectl get pvc pgdata -o jsonpath=\\",
            "  '{.status.capacity.storage}'",
            "# 50Gi  <- resize finished"
          ],
          "note": "spec says 50Gi long before status does"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Snapshots: The Second Triple",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Storage",
            "Snapshot",
            "Scope"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "PVC",
              "VolumeSnapshot",
              "namespaced"
            ],
            [
              "PV",
              "VolumeSnapshotContent",
              "cluster"
            ],
            [
              "StorageClass",
              "VolumeSnapshotClass",
              "cluster"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 0,
          "frame": "solid"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "yaml",
          "lines": [
            "spec:",
            "  dataSource:      # restore",
            "    name: pg-snap-mon",
            "    kind: VolumeSnapshot",
            "    apiGroup: snapshot.storage.k8s.io",
            "  resources: {requests: {storage: 50Gi}}"
          ],
          "note": "kind: PersistentVolumeClaim = clone"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Cloning a Live PVC",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`dataSource` pointing at another **PVC** copies it live",
            "__Same StorageClass and same namespace only__",
            "No snapshot object in between — driver copies directly",
            "Handy for {green:staging from prod} or a debug replica"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Crash-consistent, not app-consistent",
          "text": "A snapshot is a **power-cut** image of the disk. Quiesce writes or use `pg_dump` / the engine's own backup when you need a transactional guarantee."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "A __Deployment__ shares one PVC across every replica; a __StatefulSet__ hands each pod its ==own volume== through `volumeClaimTemplates`, plus a stable name.",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Example : `postgres-1` restarts on another node and reattaches `data-postgres-1` — same rows, same disk.",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "pink"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "kubernetes",
      "subtitle": "Container Storage Interface"
    }
